## Root Cause Analysis & Prescribed Fix (AUTHORITATIVE — start here, do not re-trace)
A code investigation already traced this bug to its cause and prescribed the minimal fix below. This is the plan of record. Apply it; do NOT re-read the whole codebase to re-derive it.

The Acceptance Criteria above describe the desired END BEHAVIOR to VERIFY — they are NOT an implementation blueprint. Do not re-architect, split values, or add new fields/abstractions to satisfy an AC literally when the prescribed minimal fix already makes that AC pass. Implement the fix below; the ACs are how you check you got it right.

HARD RULES:
- Make the SMALLEST change that fixes the root cause. Fewer lines of code is always better.
- REUSE existing functions. Before writing any new helper, search the repo for an existing util/parser/formatter that already does what you need (use the CodeGraph tool documented below) and call it. Writing novel code when a helper already exists is a defect to be rejected in review.
- **src/services/submit-reservations/apply-report-discounts.service.ts** (`applyReportDiscountsService`): This is the code that COMPUTES/ASSIGNS the promo (Code) discount onto the Mozio dispatch payload (dispatch.report.price.discount) that feeds the Mozio email confirmation. The matching filter `dispatch.lineItems.some((lineItem) => lineItem.id === discount.lineItemId)` compares the raw dispatch line-item id against the order line-item id. For Return trip tickets the dispatch line-item id was built by getDispatchLineItemKey as `${id}#return` (RETURN_TRIP_TAIL in src/services/helpers/order/dispatch-line-item-key.ts), so the strict equality never matches for return-trip dispatches, discountsForDispatch is empty, and the promo amount is never written into dispatch.report.price.discount — hence it is missing from the Mozio email for Return trips only.
  - **Minimal fix:** In applyReportDiscountsService (src/services/submit-reservations/apply-report-discounts.service.ts), change the matching expression `dispatch.lineItems.some((lineItem) => lineItem.id === discount.lineItemId)` to parse the dispatch key first, e.g. `dispatch.lineItems.some((lineItem) => parseDispatchLineItemKey(lineItem.id).id === discount.lineItemId)`. Reuse the EXISTING helper parseDispatchLineItemKey, imported from `~/services/helpers/order/dispatch-line-item-key` (it splits off the `#return` RETURN_TRIP_TAIL), so return-trip dispatch line items (`id#return`) match their order line-item id and the discount/promo amount is computed and assigned exactly as it already is for one-way trips. No other logic change is needed.


## Verification Criteria (what a tester will CONFIRM — your change must satisfy every one)
These are observable checks, derived from the acceptance criteria and description. They describe WHAT is observed, not how to build it. Make the minimal change that makes all of these true; your accompanying test should assert them:
- The promo code discount amount shown in the Mozio email confirmation for a return trip ticket displays the correct value for that return trip
- The promo code discount amount shown in the Mozio email confirmation for an outbound (non-return) trip ticket remains correct and unchanged
- The promo code discount name shown in the Mozio email confirmation for both outbound and return trip tickets remains correctly masked and displayed

